Z||000004||sqoach||10-24-2001||08:14 PM||||Burn all through 1st with a 2.5!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>My V6 can't even do that. It can spin 'em for a while, but not all the way through 1st. Sure, my 2.5L 5spd can spin the tires, but not a whole lot. Never able to get it to chirp 2nd. Not enough power. I didn't try much either cuz I didn't like going past 4500 rpms on it. Do you guys have skinny tires or something? 175s?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||10-25-2001||01:39 AM||||I'm going to take a recording of it. I'll post it in the next week or so. I was suprised when I did this with my duke. Keep in mind I was beating the living crap out of the clutch and slaming into 2nd gear, I didnt just punch it from a rolling or anything  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. This is also with 205/55-16 tires.<P>I think if you really try hard enough you can get just about any car to lay down some rubber  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">! I have not driven one yet that wouldn't. Was a bit tricky/almost impossable in my 88 coupe auto though...||||reg||6
Z||000006||Neal||10-25-2001||01:52 AM||||Hmmm ive driven a few cars that just wont lay any rubber...<P>dropped the clutch at 4500 and the car nearly stalled, on a fiero V6 with a hurting but running engine. <BR>When i rebuilt that engine it was a bloddy strong 2.8 but still wouldnt do more than a healthy chirp and it would easily let a chirp into second. tires were 225 15's||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kelvin Vivian||10-25-2001||02:45 AM||||In the Motor Trend Fiero video, one of the segments includes a 0-60 mph testing of a 4-cyl, 4-spd 84. They revved the engine, dropped the clutch and had a little burnout going for about 1/2 a second and you can hear a chirp into second, so I am a believer of Dukes being able to burnout with a dropping of the clutch.<P>I love the Duke and the V6 too.<BR>KV<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<BR>88 GT T-Top, 5-spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=0&courtesy=1"> <BR>The 87 4-cyl...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
