Z||000012||Master_Sushi||10-26-2001||01:53 PM||||"" Anyways, dropping the clutch is reving the motor than poping the clutch pedal out, right? I try that and it almost stales out... ""<P>Yup, thats poping the clutch. Not to good for the clutch though, expecially on fieros. If done to often im sure the clutch would frag itself, or just burn up. My fieros got almost 100k on it now. I need to rev to like 3K and drop the clutch on mine, otherwise it will stall out. My fieros kind of just a winter beater. So if it makes it through the winter with minimal repairs I'll be happy. Depending on what shape its in, it will either be parted out or sold complete in spring!<P>Nothings more fun then abusing a car you dont care about!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||12
